From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: video processor enumerator, processor, views and context state (3730)

d3d11: video processor enumerator, processor, views and context state

Adds dlls/d3d11/videoproc.c: ID3D11VideoProcessorEnumerator(1), ID3D11VideoProcessor,
the processor input and output views, and the 52 ID3D11VideoContext
VideoProcessorSet*/Get* accessors, which keep their state on the processor object
(unaffected by ClearState) with the documented defaults. The caps are the truthful
ones for a build with no video processing back end: no feature, filter, format or
stereo capability, one rate conversion group, 16 stream states, no input stream.
The video device answers the decoder profile/config/format/content-protection
queries (nothing supported), forwards its private data to the device, and decoders
return the description and configuration they were created with. Decoder output
views hold their resource and description.
